    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the following system of linear inequalities graphically:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle y \le {@eq1@} \)<br>
\( \displaystyle y > {@eq2@} \)
</p>

<p><b>a)</b> Find the exact coordinate point where the two boundary lines \( y = {@eq1@} \) and \( y = {@eq2@} \) intersect.</p>
<p><i>(Enter the numerical values for the coordinates below.)</i></p>

<p>\(x\)-coordinate: \( x = \) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<p>\(y\)-coordinate: \( y = \) [[input:ans2]]</p>

<div><b>\(x\)-coordinate check:</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div><b>\(y\)-coordinate check:</b> [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>b)</b> Graph the system of inequalities on the Cartesian plane below:</p>
<ul>
<li>Drag the <b>two blue points</b> to set the boundary line for \( y \le {@eq1@} \). <i>(This line is solid)</i>.</li>
<li>Drag the <b>two red points</b> to set the boundary line for \( y > {@eq2@} \). <i>(This line is dashed)</i>.</li>
<li>Drag the <b>green Region Marker</b> strictly into the overlapping feasible region that satisfies both inequalities.</li>
</ul>

