    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: The Algebraic Intersection</b></p>
<p>To find the exact point where the boundary lines intersect, we equate the two linear expressions.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@eq1@} &= {@eq2@} \\
{@m1@}x - {@m2@}x &= {@c2@} - {@c1@} \\
{@m1 - m2@}x &= {@c2 - c1@} \\
x &= {@ta1@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>
<p>We substitute this \(x\)-value back into either boundary equation to find the corresponding \(y\)-coordinate.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
y &= {@m1@}({@ta1@}) + {@c1@} \\
y &= {@ta2@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>
<p>The two boundary lines intersect exactly at \(({@ta1@}, {@ta2@})\).</p>

<p><b>Part b: Graphical Representation</b></p>
<p>We plot the two boundary lines on the Cartesian plane. The blue line for \( y \le {@eq1@} \) is solid, and we shade the region below it. The red line for \( y &gt; {@eq2@} \) is dashed, and we shade the region above it.</p>
<p>The feasible region is the specific area where these two shaded regions overlap. Testing a coordinate point in each quadrant formed by the intersection confirms the correct overlapping area.</p>

[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="400px"]]
var m1 = {#m1#};
var c1 = {#c1#};
var m2 = {#m2#};
var c2 = {#c2#};
var rx = {#ta7[1]#};
var ry = {#ta7[2]#};

var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-11, 11, 11, -11],
    axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});

var xaxis = brd.create('axis', [[0, 0], [1, 0]], {
    name: 'x', withLabel: true, label: {position: 'rt', offset: [-15, 20]},
    firstArrow: true, lastArrow: true, strokeWidth: 1.5,
    ticks: {
        drawLabels: true, label: {offset: [-8, -15]}, drawZero: true, insertTicks: false,
        ticksDistance: 2, minorTicks: 1,
        majorHeight: -1, minorHeight: -1,
        strokeColor: '#a0a0a0', strokeOpacity: 0.5, strokeWidth: 1,
        minorStrokeColor: '#e0e0e0', minorStrokeOpacity: 0.5, minorStrokeWidth: 1
    }
});

var yaxis = brd.create('axis', [[0, 0], [0, 1]], {
    name: 'y', withLabel: true, label: {position: 'rt', offset: [15, -15]},
    firstArrow: true, lastArrow: true, strokeWidth: 1.5,
    ticks: {
        drawLabels: true, label: {offset: [-25, -5]}, drawZero: false, insertTicks: false,
        ticksDistance: 2, minorTicks: 1,
        majorHeight: -1, minorHeight: -1,
        strokeColor: '#a0a0a0', strokeOpacity: 0.5, strokeWidth: 1,
        minorStrokeColor: '#e0e0e0', minorStrokeOpacity: 0.5, minorStrokeWidth: 1
    }
});

/* Plot Line 1 (Blue, Solid, Shade Below) */
var p1_ws = brd.create('point', [0, c1], {visible: false});
var p2_ws = brd.create('point', [1, m1 + c1], {visible: false});
var line1_ws = brd.create('line', [p1_ws, p2_ws], {strokeWidth: 3, strokeColor: '#1565c0', dash: 0});
var ineq1 = brd.create('inequality', [line1_ws], {fillColor: '#1565c0', fillOpacity: 0.2, inverse: false});

/* Plot Line 2 (Red, Dashed, Shade Above) */
var p3_ws = brd.create('point', [0, c2], {visible: false});
var p4_ws = brd.create('point', [1, m2 + c2], {visible: false});
var line2_ws = brd.create('line', [p3_ws, p4_ws], {strokeWidth: 3, strokeColor: '#c62828', dash: 2});
var ineq2 = brd.create('inequality', [line2_ws], {fillColor: '#c62828', fillOpacity: 0.2, inverse: true});

/* Feasible Region Marker */
brd.create('point', [rx, ry], {name: 'Feasible Region', size: 6, strokeColor: '#2e7d32', fillColor: '#4caf50', fixed: true});
[[/jsxgraph]]]]></text>
